 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "The diagonal on a mixed open",
 "statement": "Let $X=U\\cup V$ be an open cover over $S$. The pullback of\n$\\Delta_{X/S}$ to $U\\times_SV$ is canonically the map\n\n$$\nU\\cap V\\longrightarrow U\\times_SV.\n$$\n\nThe analogous assertion holds over $V\\times_SU$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-common/lemma-nagata-diagonal-mixed-open.md",
  "place": "node lemma-nagata-diagonal-mixed-open, order 235"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Both schemes represent triples consisting of a point of $U$, a point of\n$V$, and an equality of their images in $X$. The canonical isomorphism is\nobtained from the universal property of the pullback.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
